# 301s for every URL the Squarespace site exposed, so nothing 404s
# after the cutover. Generated from the old sitemap — see NOTES.md.
#
# The trailing "!" forces each rule. astro.config.mjs mirrors this map and emits
# a meta-refresh stub at the same paths as a fallback for hosts that ignore this
# file; on Netlify a real file at the path wins over a redirect rule unless the
# rule is forced, so without the "!" every one of these would serve the stub
# instead of a genuine 301. Google follows both, but only one passes full link
# equity, and these paths carry the old site's only search ranking.

/blog/category/Info  /blog  301!
/blog/tag/auto+detailing  /blog  301!
/blog/tag/auto+detailing+tips  /blog  301!
/blog/tag/car+care+st.+louis  /blog  301!
/blog/tag/car+care+tips  /blog  301!
/blog/tag/car+detailing+near+me  /blog  301!
/blog/tag/car+detailing+schedule  /blog  301!
/blog/tag/mobile+detailing+St.+Louis  /blog  301!
/blog/tag/paint+protection  /blog  301!
/blog/tag/regular+car+detailing  /blog  301!
/blog/tag/resale+value  /blog  301!
/blog/tag/seasonal+car+care  /blog  301!
/blog/tag/st+louis  /blog  301!
/blog/tag/vehicle+maintenance  /blog  301!
/blog/tag/vehicle+protection  /blog  301!
/cart  /store  301!
/home  /  301!
/store/p/level-i-the-tune-up  /#services  301!

# Catch anything else Squarespace generated under these prefixes.
/blog/tag/*  /blog  301!
/blog/category/*  /blog  301!
/store/p/*  /#services  301!
